# Selection dialog list rows

Related: [item-list skill](../skills/item-list/SKILL.md), [dialog-windows.mdc](dialog-windows.mdc), [core-hosted-peer-dialog](../skills/core-hosted-peer-dialog/SKILL.md).

Canonical reference: `data/frontend/src/features/tags/components/TagPickerPanel.tsx`.

Also: `LibraryPickerPanel.tsx`, `CatalogLibrarySelectEmbedPage.tsx`, `UserSelectionDialog.tsx`, `UserPickerPage.tsx`, `RoleSelectionDialog.tsx`, Media `ScopedFolderBrowser` list view.

## Required — show the selected item

In **any selection / picker dialog** (standalone `CustomDialog` or peer-dialog embed body), each selected row must be visually obvious:

| Signal | Required |
|--------|----------|
| Active border | `itemListRowActiveClassName` (`border-primary`) on `ItemListItem` (or `border-primary` on custom picker cards) |
| Check icon (right) | Lucide `Check` trailing after content (rightmost before any 3-dot menu) |

**Border alone is not enough** — always render the Check when selected.

**Media thumb / grid pickers:** keep ring/border selection **and** show a small Lucide `Check` overlay on the selected tile (bottom-right of the thumb).

```tsx
const isSelected = selected?.id === item.id // or selectedIds.has(item.id)

<ItemListItem
  role="button"
  tabIndex={0}
  className={cn('cursor-pointer transition-colors', isSelected && itemListRowActiveClassName)}
  aria-label={`Select ${item.name}`}
  aria-pressed={isSelected} // or aria-selected for option lists
  onClick={() => select(item)}
  onKeyDown={(event) => {
    if (event.key === 'Enter' || event.key === ' ') {
      event.preventDefault()
      select(item)
    }
  }}
>
  {/* optional leading: color swatch, Avatar, ImagePreview */}
  <ItemListContent>{/* name / subtitle */}</ItemListContent>
  {/* optional middle trailing: StatusTag / badge */}
  {isSelected ? (
    <Check className="ml-auto h-5 w-5 shrink-0 self-center text-primary" aria-hidden />
  ) : null}
</ItemListItem>
```

## Layout rules

- Check is rightmost among selection indicators — after content and any badges (`StatusTag`, role chip); if the row also has `ItemListMenu`, place Check **before** the menu.
- Classes (list rows): `ml-auto h-5 w-5 shrink-0 self-center text-primary`, `aria-hidden`.
- Classes (media thumbs): `absolute` bottom-right on the tile + `text-primary`, `aria-hidden`.
- Multi-select: Check on every selected row (same icon).
- Single-select: Check only on the pending/selected row.
- Pure picker rows: no 3-dot menu required. Media browser may keep menus; Check still required when selected.

## Forbidden

- Selected state = `itemListRowActiveClassName` only (no Check)
- Check on the left, or replacing the leading entity icon/swatch
- Custom checkmarks, filled circles, or non-Lucide substitutes
- `bg-accent` / `bg-primary` fill on selected rows (border + Check only)

## Verification

```bash
npm run type-check -w webonone-v2-root   # or data-root / identity-root / ui-kit-root
```

Manual: open the picker → click a row → primary border **and** Check on the right; change selection → Check moves (single) or toggles (multi).
